<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 19 January, from 649 to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">649 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,377 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kucha surrenders to the Tang after a forty-day siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of Kucha, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> oasis state aligned with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a>, surrendered to the Tang general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a> She'er after a forty-day siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksu">Aksu</a>. The conquest established Tang control over the northern Tarim Basin.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1419">1419 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">607 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rouen surrenders to Henry V</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a six-month siege that left thousands starving, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a> yielded to Henry V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, completing his conquest of Normandy. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-troyes">Treaty of Troyes</a> in 1420 made him heir to the French throne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1421 CE <span class="tih-ago">605 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John VIII Palaiologos is crowned co-emperor beside his father Manuel II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John VIII Palaiologos, eldest son of Emperor Manuel II, married Sophia of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> and was crowned co-emperor, assuming full power. He became sole emperor on his father's death in 1425.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-palaiologos">Manuel II Palaiologos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1853">1853 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">173 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Verdi's 'Il trovatore' premieres in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Giuseppe Verdi</a>'s opera of passion and revenge opened at the Teatro <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> to great acclaim. With 'Rigoletto' and 'La traviata', it is one of the three popular masterpieces of his middle period.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelins bomb Britain for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German airships dropped bombs on Great Yarmouth, Sheringham and King's Lynn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norfolk">Norfolk</a>, killing four civilians. It was the first air raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, opening a new front in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zimmermann Telegram is forwarded to Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s ambassador in Washington relayed Arthur Zimmermann's secret offer of an alliance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, promising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. Decoded by British intelligence, its publication helped bring the US into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howard Hughes sets a transcontinental air speed record</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hughes flew his H-1 racer from Burbank, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, to Newark, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, in 7 hours, 28 minutes and 25 seconds. The record stood for seven years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi chosen to lead India</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress parliamentary party elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> as its leader after the sudden death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lal-bahadur-shastri">Lal Bahadur Shastri</a>. Sworn in five days later, she became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first and only woman prime minister.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1983">1983 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">43 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apple announces the Lisa computer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Apple unveiled the Lisa, a personal computer with a graphical interface and a mouse. At nearly 10,000 dollars it sold poorly, but its ideas fed directly into the Macintosh a year later.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 19 January <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-watt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-watt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Watt</span><span class="tp">1736–1819</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-e-lee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert E. Lee</span><span class="tp">1807–1870</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/javier-perez-de-cuellar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/javier-perez-de-cuellar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Javier Pérez de Cuéllar</span><span class="tp">1920–2020</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 19 January <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dagobert-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dagobert I</span><span class="tp">c. 603–639</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hans-sachs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hans-sachs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hans Sachs</span><span class="tp">1494–1576</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maharana-pratap"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maharana-pratap.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maharana Pratap</span><span class="tp">1540–1597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-joseph-proudhon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-joseph-proudhon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre-Joseph Proudhon</span><span class="tp">1809–1865</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hoffmann-von-fallersleben"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hoffmann-von-fallersleben.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hoffmann von Fallersleben</span><span class="tp">1798–1874</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-mitre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bartolome-mitre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bartolomé Mitre</span><span class="tp">1821–1906</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
